   "t": "Настя, что ты сейчас делаешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nastya, what are you doing now?' A plain question to set up the shock. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "делаешь?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", 'you do', ends in -esh, the regular ending when you talk to one person as ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "ты",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Ну, у нас же настоящее свидание!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, we are on a real date!' adds 'obviously', as if Max ought ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "же",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to know. ",
